<%#
  THE GROUPED PAGE, ONE SHAPE FOR THE MAKER'S PAGE AND THE VISITOR'S (2026-09-09, tabs; spec §6).
  A LAYOUT PARTIAL: the caller renders it with a block that takes a KEY and returns that key's
  slot markup (or nothing), so each page keeps its own way of rendering a panel while the shape
  around the panels is written once.

  THE NO-TABS BRANCH IS TODAY'S MARKUP, UNCHANGED (decision 9): one `.project-panels` grid with
  every key and the caller's tail (the public page's repository cards) inside
  it. Every existing project takes this branch. The one addition is a SHELF GROUP's heading
  (2026-10-20, ProjectsHelper#panels_with_group_heads), drawn only before panels whose folder's
  shelf is in a group -- a user with no groups gets exactly the markup above.

  WITH TABS: the top group's grid (omitted when empty), then `div.tabs` with a bar and one pane per
  tab, then the tail in its own grid, so it is on view whichever tab is open (decision 3; Publish
  sat in that foot too until it left the page for the edit area's Publishing tab, 2026-10-26).
  A PANE IS RENDERED ONLY IF SOMETHING IN IT RENDERS: the bodies are captured
  first, exactly as the public page has always omitted an empty panel, and the bar lists only the
  panes that survived. Each key is yielded ONCE.

  THE LINK'S ID IS `tablink-<slug>` AND THE PANE'S IS `tab-<slug>`, WHICH IS NOT A COSMETIC CHOICE:
  the pane of a tab NAMED "build tab" is `tab-build-tab`, so an `id` built as `tab-<slug>-tab` for
  the link would collide with it and `aria-labelledby` would point at a pane instead of its own
  label. Two prefixes cannot collide whatever anyone names a tab.

  WITHOUT JAVASCRIPT nothing is hidden: the bar's links are anchors to the panes and every pane
  shows its heading -- the page reads as sections. tabs_controller.js hides the rest (decision 8).

  SHELF-GROUP HEADINGS ARE PER GRID (2026-10-20): the top group and each pane are each one call to
  ProjectsHelper#panels_with_group_heads (the foot holds only the tail, never in a
  group), so a run of a group's panels gets one heading in each grid it lands in.

  Locals: groups (Maker::ProjectKind::Groups); layout (the Maker::ProjectKind::Layout the groups
  came from -- the maker's @panel_layout or the visitor's pub.layout); tail (HTML or nil).
%>
<% if groups.tabs.empty? %>
  <div class="project-panels" data-controller="masonry">
    <%= panels_with_group_heads(groups.top, layout) { |key| yield key } %>
    <%= tail %>
  </div>
<% else %>
  <% panes = groups.tabs.filter_map do |tab|
       body = panels_with_group_heads(tab.keys, layout) { |key| yield key }
       [ tab, body ] if body.present?
     end %>
  <%# THE HEAD IS KEYED ON WHAT RENDERED, LIKE THE FOOT (found in review): a visitor's top group may
      hold only keys with no public face (Tasks, Sheets), and a grid with nothing in it is a blank
      band above the bar. %>
  <% head = panels_with_group_heads(groups.top, layout) { |key| yield key } %>
  <% if head.present? %>
    <div class="project-panels" data-controller="masonry"><%= head %></div>
  <% end %>
  <% if panes.any? %>
    <div class="tabs" data-controller="tabs">
      <nav class="tab-bar" role="tablist" aria-label="Page sections">
        <% panes.each_with_index do |(tab, _body), i| %>
          <a class="tab-link" role="tab" id="tablink-<%= tab.slug %>" href="#tab-<%= tab.slug %>"
             aria-controls="tab-<%= tab.slug %>" aria-selected="<%= i.zero? %>" tabindex="<%= i.zero? ? 0 : -1 %>"
             data-tabs-target="tab" data-action="click->tabs#select keydown->tabs#key"><%= tab.name %></a>
        <% end %>
      </nav>
      <% panes.each do |tab, body| %>
        <section class="tab-pane" id="tab-<%= tab.slug %>" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tablink-<%= tab.slug %>" data-tabs-target="pane">
          <h2 class="tab-heading"><%= tab.name %></h2>
          <div class="project-panels" data-controller="masonry"><%= body %></div>
        </section>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
  <% if tail.present? %>
    <div class="project-panels" data-controller="masonry"><%= tail %></div>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
